I agree with the direction. The pilot was too small to generalize from a single badger run, and the current contract overstates what is proven. The six priorities are sound: treat head/body split as unverified, fix T0 as a real gate, add a minimal animation check before fine rigging, allow uniform transform conventions instead of banning all constant rotations, make visual checks deterministic and multi-view, and measure actual rework saved rather than just pixel scores. I would also keep the 12-image / 150-point cap for now, confirm T3 rigging cost, and write licensing as preserve source and usage records plus re-check when code, skills, or assets are introduced.
